{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"@'\nimport subprocess,tomllib,json\nrev='4ed1d5b49e2379b265f9609791013483be7907fe'\nfor path,ids in [('docs/requirements/system-requirements.toml',['SR-186']),('docs/requirements/stakeholder-needs.toml',['SN-012','SN-040']),('docs/requirements/interfaces.toml',['IF-035','IF-262','IF-019','IF-254','IF-097','IF-098'])]:\n data=tomllib.loads(subprocess.check_output(['git','show',rev+':'+path]).decode())\n for key in ids:\n  for group in data.values():\n   if isinstance(group,dict) and key in group:\n    print(key,json.dumps(group[key],ensure_ascii=True))\n'@ | python -\"","aggregated_output":"SR-186 {\"title\": \"Proportionate requirement decomposition\", \"sn_refs\": [\"SN-012\"], \"boundary_refs\": [\"B-05\"], \"hat_refs\": [\"MAINTAINER\", \"PRODUCT-FITNESS\"], \"requirement\": \"The delivered requirements process shall require each additional child within a required tier to carry an independent decision or verification purpose, and record the stopping decision in the scoped decomposition record, while retaining the required SN-to-SR-to-LLR-to-TC tiers and linking real verification to the existing obligation.\", \"rationale\": \"Carries SN-012's unowned granularity clause as a process requirement on what the delivered process requires and records. A child that only paraphrases a parent or duplicates another child's verification adds review and maintenance cost without an independent decision. The process records the stopping decision within the required spine; this row does not guarantee adopter behavior beyond that record, and it never permits omitting a required SN\\u2192SR\\u2192LLR\\u2192TC tier or replacing real verification with a count. It does not impose a row-count cap, deletion quota, or new machine gate. Existing process doctrine and the spine-authoring adjudicator questions are the source of the judgment, while mechanism-specific evidence remains with its current SR.\", \"acceptance_criteria\": \"For a reviewed decomposition, each additional child within a required tier has an independent decision or verification purpose traceable to its parent; when further splitting would only paraphrase or duplicate, the existing scoped decomposition/review record states why the process stops at that independent-value boundary.\", \"priority\": \"S\", \"verification\": \"Inspection\", \"status\": \"Approved\", \"phase\": 5, \"coincident\": \"The need asks for a decomposition that stays proportionate; each additional child's recorded purpose, and the recorded stopping decision, is that outcome, judged by review.\", \"aspect\": \"process\"}\r\nSN-012 {\"status\": \"Approved\", \"stakeholder_refs\": [\"STK-02\"], \"tags\": [\"process\"], \"need\": \"A team can keep small changes small: the process is **right-sized**, not ceremony for its own sake \\u2014 small changes stay cheap, and heavy layers are opt-in.\", \"why\": \"An over-heavy process is abandoned; adoption depends on proportionality.\", \"priority\": \"S\", \"acceptance\": \"Opt-in layers (perf, guardrails, unattended, parallel tracks, OKF export) cost a repo that doesn't use them nothing; the proportionality doctrine governs LLR/TC granularity.\"}\r\nSN-040 {\"status\": \"Approved\", \"stakeholder_refs\": [\"STK-03\"], \"priority\": \"S\", \"need\": \"**Scope: template (adopters + this repo).** A stakeholder can obtain a repeatable explanation for why the system was divided into its chosen components, based on the system's declared inputs, outputs and internal signal trade-offs rather than an unrecorded model judgment.\", \"why\": \"A component breakdown invented free-form by a model (or a person) leaves no record of the alternatives weighed, so the next reviser cannot tell load-bearing boundaries from accidents. Deriving the partition from the system's own declared inputs and outputs, against a declared objective, leaves evidence the choice can be re-examined against.\", \"acceptance\": \"A decomposition run records the candidate partitions considered, the declared objective and constraints they were scored against, the selected partition, and a comparison a reviewer can reproduce; the human names the components and rules the final choice; the record is kept with the architecture, not in session prose.\"}\r\nIF-035 {\"owner\": \"project-trajectory/skills/\", \"consumers\": [\"scripts/gen_skills_index\", \"scripts/bootstrap\"], \"channel\": \"file\", \"data\": \"SKILL.md frontmatter: name, scope, stacks, domains, phases, tags; each other file in the skill directory, materialized with it at the same relative path\", \"version\": \"v1\", \"status\": \"Drafted\", \"notes\": \"Low fan-out: two direct walkers of a skill directory - bootstrap (select_skills filtering on the SKILL.md frontmatter at scaffold time, then skill_copies materializing and inventorying the whole directory) and gen_skills_index (the INDEX.csv generator, and the fan-out drift check comparing the whole file set). A closed, nameable set.\"}\r\nIF-262 {\"owner\": \"scripts/kitlib/bootstrap_manifest\", \"requestors\": [\"scripts/bootstrap\"], \"channel\": \"call\", \"data\": \"MAPPING and mapping_entries: the ordered scaffold source, destination, and optional requirement-reference inventory\", \"version\": \"v1\", \"status\": \"Drafted\", \"component\": \"CMP-009\"}\r\nIF-019 {\"owner\": \"scripts/gen_skills_index\", \"consumers\": [\"external:downstream adopter\"], \"channel\": \"file\", \"data\": \"skills/INDEX.csv: banner comment, header, one row per skill (name, scope, stacks, domains, phases, tags, description)\", \"version\": \"v1\", \"status\": \"Drafted\", \"interface_to_external\": \"B-05\", \"coincident\": \"The index row per skill is what an agent or a person reads to find a skill; the listing is the outcome.\"}\r\nIF-254 {\"owner\": \"scripts/gen_skills_index\", \"consumers\": [\"scripts/check\"], \"channel\": \"exit-code\", \"data\": \"--check: 0 index fresh and descriptions at or over the floor, or no skills dir \\u00b7 1 stale index or a description under the floor\", \"version\": \"v1\", \"status\": \"Drafted\", \"component\": \"CMP-009\"}\r\nIF-097 {\"owner\": \"scripts/prompts\", \"requestors\": [\"scripts/agent_loop\", \"scripts/plan_briefs\"], \"channel\": \"call\", \"data\": \"load | fill | preflight | digest | template_path | strip_dispatcher_block; KIT_PROMPTS | KIT_FRAGMENTS | SPINE_QUESTIONS\", \"version\": \"v1\", \"status\": \"Drafted\", \"component\": \"CMP-008\", \"notes\": \"source: the templates are files under project-trajectory/prompts/, not code.\"}\r\nIF-098 {\"owner\": \"scripts/prompts\", \"requestors\": [\"scripts/gen_prompt_catalog\"], \"channel\": \"call\", \"data\": \"catalog_rows() -> (key, file, slots, digest); fragment_rows() -> (file, slot, digest)\", \"version\": \"v1\", \"status\": \"Drafted\", \"component\": \"CMP-009\", \"notes\": \"sink: its output is a generated DOCUMENT, not an API any module calls. Freshness-gated and declared in docs/stack.ini [generated].\"}\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
